    description: "Surfaced by WI-javan (2026-04-20): running 'pytest tests/ --no-cov' on dev (46a839f75) yields 3 failures that CI never caught because neither full-suite.yml nor ci.yml run the top-level tests/ directory. All three are real drift, not flakes:\n\n1. tests/test_generate_concepts.py::test_committed_file_is_up_to_date\n   - docs/CONCEPTS.md is stale vs the generator. Fix: run scripts/generate-concepts to regenerate and commit the output. Likely drift from a recent framework YAML or consumer change that didn't update the committed artifact.\n\n2. tests/test_training_log_parse_misses.py::TestLogTrainingExampleCohortMetadata::test_pipeline_version_is_v1\n   - Asserts entry['pipeline_version'] == 'v1', but the actual value is 'v2'. Pipeline version was bumped in .agent/hooks/_shared/on_transcript_change.py (v1 → v2) without updating this test. Fix: update the assertion to 'v2' and audit whether downstream consumers of the training log need to keep consuming v1 during a migration window (probably not — a version bump usually means consumers already moved).\n\n3. tests/test_training_log_parse_misses.py::TestLogTrainingExampleCohortMetadata::test_extra_still_works_alongside_cohort\n   - Fails at tests/test_training_log_parse_misses.py:509; same TestLogTrainingExampleCohortMetadata class as #2, likely a shared schema-drift root cause with the pipeline_version bump.\n\nAll three are blockers for landing WI-javan's full-suite.yml change — if we add a test-agent-infra job right now, full-suite goes red immediately. Fix these, then land WI-javan (or invert: land WI-javan with these tests xfailed and clear the xfails here)."  # f2c3
    fields: {}  # f2c3
